BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Friends of Brown County State Park Monthly Meeting\, Brown County 
 State Park
DTSTART;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260603T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Indiana/Indianapolis:20260603T200000
UID:d6d76b2488df45f54e8b7106dd03e276@events.in.gov
DESCRIPTION:The Friends of Brown County State Park is a not for profit org
 anization that fundraises for park infrastructure\, plans events\, and org
 anizes volunteer work. Come learn how you can be involved with Brown Count
 y State Park! The meeting begins at 6:30pm at the Brown County State Park 
 Nature Center. Meetings are the first Wednesday of every month. The Friend
 s help with the Wildflower Foray\, Rockfest\, Snakefest\, Halloween\, and 
 other events! Completed projects include the Friends Trail\, the Friends&#
 39\; Picnic Shelter near the Nature Center\, the restored Peach Tree Shelt
 er\, the pickel ball courts\, the flower gardens around the park\, and man
 y other projects! Get involved now to help with the restoration of the Fir
 e Tower. The goal is to have the work done by the Brown County State Park 
 Centennial in 2029. Learn more about the Friends by coming to the meeting 
 or visiting their website: https://www.friendsbcsp.org/
LOCATION:Brown County State Park\, Nature Center\, 1405 S.R. 46 W\, Nashvi
 lle\, IN 
URL:https://on.in.gov/browncountysp
X-SOURCE:Brown County State Park
END:VEVENT
